.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_cfg
is a typed runtime configuration registry, modeled on PostgreSQL's
GUC system.  Modules register named knobs at startup; operators
set them by name; values get bound to live variables and validated
against type and bounds.
.Pp
Supported types:
.Dv bool , int , int64 , double , string , enum .
Each
.Fn xtc_cfg_register_*
takes:
.Bl -bullet -compact -offset indent
.It
A canonical name
.Pq dot-separated, e.g. Sq rexis.max_clients .
.It
A backing storage pointer.  When the cfg value changes, the
storage is updated atomically.
.It
A default and bounds
.Pq for numeric types .
.It
A help string used in
.Sq cfg dump
output.
.El
.Pp
.Fn xtc_cfg_set
parses the string value to the registered type, validates against
bounds, and updates the backing variable.  An optional on-change
callback fires.
.Pp
Modules register a knob with
.Fn xtc_cfg_register ,
passing an
.Vt xtc_cfg_spec_t
that carries name, type, backing storage, default and bounds; the
type-specific
.Fn xtc_cfg_register_bool ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_register_int ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_register_int64 ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_register_double ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_register_string ,
and
.Fn xtc_cfg_register_enum
wrappers fill that spec for one type.
.Fn xtc_cfg_unregister
removes a knob by name.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_cfg_set
parses the string value to the registered type, validates against
bounds, and updates the backing variable.  An optional on-change
callback fires.  The typed setters
.Fn xtc_cfg_set_bool ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_set_int ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_set_int64 ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_set_double ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_set_string ,
and
.Fn xtc_cfg_set_enum
assign a value of the matching C type without going through the
string parser.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_cfg_get
.Pq via the typed accessors
reads the current value.  Use
.Fn xtc_cfg_get_bool ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_get_int ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_get_int64 ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_get_double ,
.Fn xtc_cfg_get_string ,
or
.Fn xtc_cfg_get_enum
for the corresponding registered kind.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_cfg_count
returns the number of registered knobs;
.Fn xtc_cfg_kind
reports the
.Vt xtc_cfg_kind_t
type of a named knob.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static int g_max_clients = 1000;

xtc_cfg_register_int("rexis.max_clients", &g_max_clients,
                      1000, 1, 100000,
                      "Maximum concurrent client connections");

/* Operator runtime change: */
xtc_cfg_set("rexis.max_clients", "5000");
.Ed
